Package: netRobust
Title: Network Robustness Under Random Failures and Targeted Attacks
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Manuel J.", "Zetina-Rejon", , "mjzetina@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates and compares network robustness to random node
    failures and targeted attacks (by degree, betweenness, closeness,
    eigenvector centrality, and PageRank), extending the approach of
    Albert, Jeong & Barabasi (2000) <doi:10.1038/35019019>. Includes a
    Monte Carlo framework for testing whether an attack scenario is
    statistically more damaging than random failure, and utilities for
    plotting robustness curves with a null-model reference envelope.
